schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-creature-false-survivor
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Dark fantasy concept art of the False Survivor — an ambient enemy found in Zone 7,
    the Plane of Echoes. This creature is a mirror copy of the player character — same
    worn leather coat, same alchemical tool belt, same amber lantern — but everything is
    subtly wrong in ways that escalate the longer you look. The coat is buttoned on the
    wrong side. The tools on the belt are in reversed order. The lantern glows with a
    cold blue-white light instead of amber. The face is the player's face but the
    expression is wrong — a smile that doesn't reach the eyes, or eyes that track
    independently. The proportions are fractionally off — slightly too tall, hands slightly
    too large, fingers one knuckle too long. The stance mirrors the player's but is
    performed with the rehearsed quality of an actor copying mannerisms they don't
    understand. Most unsettling: where the player has accumulated damage and wear from
    their journey — scorch marks, repaired tears in the coat, a cracked vial — the False
    Survivor has these details in the wrong places, as if guessing at the player's history.
    It stands in a fractured reflection of the player's environment — everything inverted,
    the Plane of Echoes pressing in around it. The mood is the uncanny valley weaponized —
    something that looks almost exactly like you, enough to trigger recognition but not
    enough to pass.
  negative: "bright, cheerful, cartoon, anime, clean magic, obvious monster, demon, doppelganger traditional, generic evil twin, colorful palette, symmetrical to player, low detail, flat shading"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1024
    height: 1536
    aspect_ratio: "2:3"

tags: [creature, ambient-enemy, zone-7, mirror, false-player, uncanny, concept-art, dark-fantasy]
